
                                                   READDATA COMMAND


READDATA command can be used to read data from a hex file with a particular address and length. 

Below is the syntax :
                                readdata -in hexfile [-igCks {"true"|"false"}] -addr address  [-l len]  [-fill fillGapValue]

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES       |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -in         |    "-in" takes input hex file to be read. Supports Intel(".hex"), Motorola(".s19") and
               |    Binary(".bin"). Mandatory switch.
   -igcks      |    Ignores wrong line checksum of input hex file when set to TRUE. By default set to FALSE.
               |    Optional switch.
   -addr       |    Takes address value such as 0x80000000. Mandatory switch.
   -l          |    Specifies length of data to be read. By default it reads only one byte. Optional switch. 
   -fill       |    Fills gaps with the one byte pattern provided. Optional switch.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:
    readdata -in input.hex -igCks true
    readdata -in input.hex -addr 0x80800000 -l 0x20 -fill 0xAE